# Docker Colima Setup

## When to Apply

- Any task that builds or runs Docker images in this repo.
- Any task involving `docker compose`, `docker buildx`, or Colima.
- Any Docker failure that mentions missing Compose/Buildx plugins, public
  registry certificate errors, or localhost port forwarding not working.

## Baseline Checks

Start with Docker, not Colima, because Colima status can be less useful than the
Docker daemon state on this machine:

```bash
docker info
docker ps --format '{{.Names}} {{.Ports}}'
colima status
```

Expected Docker context:

```text
Context: colima
```

Do not stop or restart Colima just because a command is confusing. There may be
unrelated containers running, such as `wiremock-simulator` on port `9999`.

## Install Docker Compose and Buildx Plugins

If these fail:

```bash
docker compose version
docker buildx version
```

install the Homebrew plugin packages:

```bash
brew install docker-compose docker-buildx
```

Then ensure Docker can discover Homebrew's plugin directory. Update
`~/.docker/config.json` to include:

```json
{
  "cliPluginsExtraDirs": [
    "/opt/homebrew/lib/docker/cli-plugins"
  ]
}
```

Verify:

```bash
docker info
```

Expected plugin lines include:

```text
Plugins:
  buildx: Docker Buildx
  compose: Docker Compose
```

## Corporate Registry and CA Pattern

Public Docker Hub and GHCR pulls can fail from Colima with:

```text
tls: failed to verify certificate: x509: certificate signed by unknown authority
```

Use the internal image mirror by default:

```text
docker.io/library/python:3.12-slim
docker.io/astral/uv:0.11.19
```

For Python dependency downloads inside Docker builds, pass the local corporate
CA bundle as a BuildKit secret instead of committing a certificate:

```bash
docker buildx build \
  # corporate CA bundle secret removed; use public registry \
  --load \
  -f services/intelligence/Dockerfile \
  -t study-tracker-intelligence:phase6 .
```

Dockerfile pattern:

```dockerfile
RUN uv sync --frozen --package intelligence --no-dev
```

Compose pattern:

```yaml
services:
  intelligence:
    build:
      context: .
      dockerfile: services/intelligence/Dockerfile
      args:
        PYTHON_IMAGE: ${PYTHON_IMAGE:-docker.io/library/python:3.12-slim}
        UV_IMAGE: ${UV_IMAGE:-docker.io/astral/uv:0.11.19}

```

Avoid `UV_INSECURE_HOST` or disabling TLS verification as the default fix.

## Colima Port Forwarding Gotcha

Docker can show a published port even when macOS localhost is not listening:

```bash
docker port study-planner-web-intelligence-1
lsof -nP -iTCP:8000 -sTCP:LISTEN
```

If `docker port` shows `0.0.0.0:8000->8000/tcp` but host curl fails, verify the
service from inside the container and VM before changing app code:

```bash
docker compose exec -T intelligence python -c "import urllib.request; print(urllib.request.urlopen('http://127.0.0.1:8000/health', timeout=5).read().decode())"

env LIMA_HOME=/Users/rsaji/.colima/_lima limactl shell colima ss -ltnp
env LIMA_HOME=/Users/rsaji/.colima/_lima limactl shell colima curl -sS http://127.0.0.1:8000/health
```

If the service works in the container and VM but not from macOS, create a
temporary SSH forward for verification:

```bash
ssh -F /Users/rsaji/.colima/ssh_config -N -L 127.0.0.1:8000:127.0.0.1:8000 colima
```

After verification, remove only that temporary forward:

```bash
ssh -F /Users/rsaji/.colima/ssh_config -O cancel -L 127.0.0.1:8000:127.0.0.1:8000 colima
```

Do not kill the existing `9999` SSH forward; it belongs to the WireMock
simulator.

## Standard Verification Flow

For this repo's Intelligence Service:

```bash
docker compose config
docker compose up --build -d
docker compose ps
curl -sS http://127.0.0.1:8000/health
docker compose down
```

If host curl cannot connect, use the Colima port-forwarding checks above before
touching service code.
